WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:18.185
It was Sunday morning, and Grandpa was making everyone pancakes.

2
00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:23.346
Joy was still in her pajamas and still talking about chickens.

3
00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:27.547
"This one has a blue tail," said Joy.

4
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:30.528
"And this one has feathers on its feet!"

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:32.821
Mom smiled.

6
00:00:32.841 --> 00:00:34.882
"They look like house slippers."

7
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:40.627
Grandpa gave Joy a plate of pancakes and looked over her shoulder at the catalog.

8
00:00:41.687 --> 00:00:43.549
"See that one with the black and white stripes?"

9
00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:44.490
he said.

10
00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.672
"We had a hen like that when I was a boy.

11
00:00:48.853 --> 00:00:51.615
Sometimes she slept in my lap—just like a cat."

12
00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:53.877
Dad smiled.

13
00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:58.240
"So Joy," he said, "do you think we should get some chickens?"

14
00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:03.695
Joy's eyes opened wide, and a big smile spread across her face.

15
00:01:03.715 --> 00:01:05.677
"Oh, Dad!

16
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:06.798
Could we?

17
00:01:07.338 --> 00:01:08.879
Could we buy some little chicks?"

18
00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:13.162
"They won't be little for long," warned Mom.

19
00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:15.384
"They'll become big chickens.

20
00:01:16.585 --> 00:01:17.846
Would you take care of them?

21
00:01:18.306 --> 00:01:20.308
Would you feed them and give them water?"

22
00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:23.730
"Yes, I promise," said Joy.

23
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.812
"And I'd gather the eggs too."

24
00:01:27.164 --> 00:01:31.026
"I could make some delicious omelets with those fresh eggs," said Grandpa.

25
00:01:31.046 --> 00:01:33.568
"Where's Katie?"

26
00:01:34.028 --> 00:01:35.989
asked Joy, jumping up from the table.

27
00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:40.872
She ran to the stairway and called, "Come downstairs, Katie!"

28
00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.895
Upstairs Katie didn't hear her sister.

29
00:01:47.495 --> 00:01:50.397
She was busy staring at herself in the bathroom mirror.

30
00:01:51.558 --> 00:01:55.300
Jellybean, the cat, was sitting in the doorway, licking her gray fur.

31
00:01:56.628 --> 00:02:00.011
"Here we go," Katie whispered as she picked up the scissors.

32
00:02:01.212 --> 00:02:05.216
Jellybean stopped licking and watched Katie with round, yellow eyes.

33
00:02:06.657 --> 00:02:08.358
Downstairs Dad was talking.

34
00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:12.002
"It's good for the planet when we raise our own food," he said.

35
00:02:12.022 --> 00:02:17.466
"I hope I can remember how to take care of baby chickens," said Grandpa.

36
00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:23.752
"You have to teach me, Grandpa," replied Joy as she sat back down at the table.

37
00:02:24.872 --> 00:02:27.394
She'd given up trying to get Katie's attention.

38
00:02:27.414 --> 00:02:32.496
"I'll bring home a book on the subject tomorrow," said Mom.

39
00:02:33.737 --> 00:02:36.459
She worked part-time at the Willow Creek library.

40
00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:40.541
Suddenly everyone looked up at the ceiling.

41
00:02:41.021 --> 00:02:43.602
They heard Katie's footsteps in the hallway above.

42
00:02:44.823 --> 00:02:47.425
Then they heard her pounding down the stairs.

43
00:02:47.445 --> 00:02:50.606
"Here she comes," said Joy.

44
00:02:50.626 --> 00:02:53.188
"Good morning, world!"

45
00:02:53.696 --> 00:02:56.158
Katie exclaimed as she popped into the kitchen.

46
00:02:57.339 --> 00:02:59.000
She twirled on her bare feet.

47
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.362
"Notice anything different about me?"

48
00:03:03.623 --> 00:03:07.165
Magoo, who had been napping in the corner, opened his eyes.

49
00:03:07.185 --> 00:03:13.209
"Yes, I noticed that you ran down the steps with scissors!"

50
00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:14.710
scolded Mom.

51
00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.812
"That's really dangerous."

52
00:03:18.053 --> 00:03:20.574
Katie looked down at the scissors in her hand.

53
00:03:20.594 --> 00:03:22.536
"Oops," she said.

54
00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:28.120
"Sorry." "You've done something to your hair," stated Dad.

55
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.582
"You've got bangs!"

56
00:03:31.182 --> 00:03:32.243
Joy burst out.

57
00:03:32.263 --> 00:03:35.666
"Ta-da!" exclaimed Katie.

58
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:37.788
Joy frowned.

59
00:03:37.808 --> 00:03:41.951
"But Katie," she said, "now we look different."

60
00:03:41.971 --> 00:03:45.614
"That's right," Katie said happily.

61
00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:48.977
"From now on, I'm the one with bangs."

62
00:03:50.238 --> 00:03:51.739
She sat down at the table.

63
00:03:51.759 --> 00:03:55.065
"Grandpa, may I have some pancakes, please?"

64
00:03:56.905 --> 00:04:00.006
"You did a good job, Katie," Mom commented.

65
00:04:01.386 --> 00:04:03.447
Joy looked around the table, upset.

66
00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:06.568
"But do we still look like twins?"

67
00:04:06.588 --> 00:04:09.849
"Sure you do," said Dad.

68
00:04:09.869 --> 00:04:13.069
"Nope," corrected Katie.

69
00:04:13.089 --> 00:04:15.310
"We look completely different."

70
00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.691
Then Mom spoke up.

71
00:04:17.711 --> 00:04:20.471
"Joy, tell Katie about the chickens."

72
00:04:21.692 --> 00:04:23.853
"Chickens?" repeated Katie.

73
00:04:23.873 --> 00:04:26.515
"Yes," said Joy.

74
00:04:26.535 --> 00:04:29.198
"We're getting chicks from the Cackle Farm!"

75
00:04:30.258 --> 00:04:31.720
Katie stared at her sister.

76
00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.601
"What will we have to do?"

77
00:04:33.621 --> 00:04:37.305
"Lots!" Joy was smiling again.

78
00:04:37.325 --> 00:04:41.548
"You see, they have to live indoors for a while.

79
00:04:42.669 --> 00:04:45.572
We have to keep them warm and watch them every minute."

80
00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.376
When Katie thought of the cute little chicks, she almost smiled.

81
00:04:51.468 --> 00:04:55.992
But then she remembered that she was the Donovan twin who didn't like chickens.

82
00:04:57.453 --> 00:04:59.354
Joy noticed Katie's blank expression.

83
00:04:59.374 --> 00:05:00.876
"Aren't you excited?"

84
00:05:01.336 --> 00:05:01.916
she asked.

85
00:05:03.097 --> 00:05:05.539
Katie shrugged and poured syrup on her pancakes.

86
00:05:07.021 --> 00:05:10.523
"Last chance for pancakes, folks," Grandpa announced.

87
00:05:11.764 --> 00:05:13.926
"Joy and I have to get this kitchen cleaned up.

88
00:05:14.326 --> 00:05:15.908
We've got chicken plans!"
